I ran the gates myself and verified every claim I could check. Here is what I found.

```
FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/transcript.rs:140 — `markdown()` computes the input fence from the *raw* input (`fence_width(&exchange.input)`) but writes the *stripped* input at :144 (`strip_escapes(&exchange.input).lines()`). `strip_escapes` deletes a whole CSI sequence, so it can JOIN two backtick runs that were separated by one — turning a raw longest run of 2 into a written run of exactly 3, which is the fence width. The reader closes a redblue block only on an exact run match (transcript.rs:202), so it closes on the *content* line and the exchange reads back as `""`. Reproduced on this checkout: `printf '``\033[0m`\n.export f.md\n:quit\n' | ./target/debug/rb` writes `...\n```redblue\n```\n```\n` — three fence lines for a 3-backtick content line; `read_markdown` returns `[""]` and the user's line is lost. The output side of this exact class is fixed correctly in this diff (transcript.rs:150-152 ask both the content and `fence_width` the same `rendered_output` text, per the stated principle at :250-253) — the input side was left on the raw text, so REPORT.md:151-155's claim that "a document this writer wrote reads back as the session that wrote it ... now holds" is not true for this input shape. Fix: `let fence = "`".repeat(fence_width(&crate::repl::style::strip_escapes(&exchange.input)));`. What would settle it either way: a `markdown()`+`read_markdown` round trip over an input holding backticks around an escape, which no test in either file has.
2. [MINOR] phases/phase-060/REPORT.md:96 — "6 new `#[test]` functions, 4 of them named `edge_*`" is false; all six are `edge_*` (src/repl/transcript.rs:535, :571, :595 and tests/repl_test.rs:1725, :1761, :1800). A test inventory the reviewer has to recount is not an inventory.
3. [MINOR] phases/phase-060/REPORT.md:11 — the diff is stated as "+327 −31 across 3 files" and :15 gives transcript.rs "+221 −30"; `git diff --numstat` says 220/29, 105/0, 1/1 — i.e. +326 −30 and +220 −29. Small, but it is the one number in the report that is meant to be checkable and it is wrong in both places.
4. [MINOR] phases/phase-060/REPORT.md:180 — the malformed_input row cites `edge_a_redblue_fence_inside_a_block_in_other_language_is_not_input`. No such test exists; the name is `..._in_another_language_...` (src/repl/transcript.rs:595).
